Yes, we have our own shutdown hook which should be called before the one of sling. But all JVM shutdown hooks are called in parallel.

Basically what we want to archive is to gracefully shutdown our Jetty-Server, i.e. all current connections will be handled and only after that the server should continue to shutdown. As part of our own shutdown hook we will shutdown the Framework as well.

Basically this is what we have in our Shutdown Hook:

Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(&quot;Custom Shutdown Hook&quot;)
{
	@Override
	public void run()
	{
		stopWebApi();
		stopMessaging();
		shutdownFramework();
	}
}

